{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "All 12 required pairs are retained. NOT_APPLICABLE concerns the exact gift questions; it neither rejects the independent duties nor establishes overall candidate correctness.",
    "The advertising claim's uncertainty metadata is stale: footnote 4 and surrounding marketing paragraphs are supplied. The external Advertising Guidelines and incorporated FAQs and guidance remain missing.",
    "The external Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 and the answer to question 1 of the SFC Code of Conduct FAQs issued on 30 September 2010 are missing. Can their applicable versions be supplied to verify substantive gift, discount and promotional-link classifications? No supplied dependency IDs identify them.",
    "Scope placement changes results. For a known distributor and an unoffered component, node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249 and node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b can return FALSE, while node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns OUT_OF_SCOPE. Promotional-link scope conditions in node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and both offer-level candidates similarly replace a negative answer with OUT_OF_SCOPE. Node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5 returns OUT_OF_SCOPE for an unlinked benefit rather than TRUE. Whether these exclusions match the intended question domain remains unresolved.",
    "An unknown scope returns UNKNOWN even when a known non-gift or discount would settle the corresponding unrestricted Boolean result. Repeating scope predicates in Result does not remove this distinction. These runtime conventions are not additional legal restrictions.",
    "Both offer-level candidates combine offer-level promotional linkage with existence of a non-discount gift. The source links the gifts themselves to promotion. Unless supplied classifications establish that the same gift participates in the linked promotion, a mixed offer may be overclassified. Whether offer-wide linkage establishes that connection remains unresolved.",
    "Node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 leaves component enumeration and evidential completeness implicit. Its existential fact can be FALSE only with sufficient evidence that no offered component qualifies; generic UNKNOWN semantics do not establish that completeness.",
    "The discount exception and TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT concern only the selected gift control. Neither establishes compliance with section 103 or advertising duties. Conversely, section 103 authorisation or exemption is not a stated gift exception.",
    "The circular says incentives may be gifts; it does not automatically classify every guaranteed return as a gift. Fund returns and distributor top-ups must remain distinguishable. Node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b's focus on offering is supported, but disputed attribution, agency and third-party funding arrangements remain unimplemented classification questions.",
    "The circular defines distributors within SFC-authorised fund distribution, while its quotation of paragraph 3.11 refers to investment products generally. Fund-limited facts fit the selected circular context but do not establish the full Code provision's reach.",
    "No concrete effective interval is established by the supplied units. The FAQ date identifies a referenced document, not the effective date of every rule. Applicable versions and competing temporal interpretations remain unresolved."
  ],
